>> title: Dansak
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: lamb, parsi, lentils, pumpkin, curry
>> counters: Curry House
>> aka: dhansak, dhansakh, lamb dhansak, chicken dansak, dhaansak
>> pairs-with: onion-tomato-masala, pilau-rice, kachumber
>> servings: 6
>> time: 2 hr 30 min
>> capacity: 3 — the heavy pot, sear

>> step: simmer 40 min, then beat to a purée
Simmer @toor dal{1%cup}(200 g; rinsed), @pumpkin{8%oz}(225 g; peeled, in chunks), @ground turmeric{1/2%tsp} and @water{4%cup}(950 mL) in a #pot{} ~simmer{40%min}, then beat the lot to a rough purée with a whisk.

>> step: sear 8 min in batches
Sear @lamb shoulder{2%lb}(900 g; cut in 1 1/2-in cubes) in @ghee{3%Tbs}(42 g) in a #heavy pot{} ~sear{8%min}, in two batches.

>> step: fry in 4 min
Fry @onion-tomato masala{1 1/2%cup}(360 g; the base recipe), @ground cumin{2%tsp}, @ground coriander{1%Tbs}, @Kashmiri chile powder{2%tsp} and @garam masala{1%tsp} into @&(~1)seared lamb{} ~fry{4%min}.

>> step: braise 1 hr, covered
Braise @&(~1)lamb{} with @water{1%cup}(240 mL) and @kosher salt{2%tsp} covered ~simmer{60%min}.

>> step: beat the dal in, simmer 10 min
Beat @&(~4)dal purée{} into @&(~1)braised lamb{} with @tamarind concentrate{1%Tbs}(20 g), @jaggery{2%tsp}(10 g), @kasuri methi{1%tsp}(crumbled) and @cilantro{1/4%cup}(chopped), and ~simmer{10%min}, adding water if it stops moving in the pot.

The lentils are the dish and not a thickener. Sweet sour and hot arrive at once: jaggery and tamarind together.
